message: "If you use GRFP Scorer in teaching, mentoring, or research, please cite it as below."
title: "GRFP Scorer: rubric-based formative feedback for NSF Graduate Research Fellowship statements"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Costa
    given-names: Vincent D.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5412-8945"   # replace with your ORCID iD
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/fullcolorbrain/grfp-scorer"
url: "https://fullcolorbrain.com/grfp-scorer"
keywords:
  - NSF GRFP
  - fellowship writing
  - graduate training
  - formative feedback
  - large language models
abstract: >
  A desktop application and command-line tools that score a draft NSF Graduate Research
  Fellowship Program statement against a ten-principle writing rubric, cite the sentence
  each sub-score rests on, and propose the highest-value revisions. Supports the Claude
  API (user-supplied key), a local Ollama model, or an offline lexical mode.
